---
description: Security scanning before commits
alwaysApply: true
---

Before running git commit, git push, or creating a PR, call the armis-scanner
MCP tool `scan_diff` with `staged=true` and `repo_path` set to your repo's
absolute work-tree root (the value of `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, not just
your current dir). Always pass `repo_path`: the MCP server's own working
directory may be a different checkout than yours (in a git worktree it is often
the main repo), so without it the scan and its `.scan-pass` land in the wrong
git dir and the commit gate never sees them. If HIGH/CRITICAL findings exist, fix them or
ask the user for approval before proceeding.

To suppress a reviewed false positive, add an `armis:ignore` comment on the
finding's line (optionally `armis:ignore cwe:798`) or list it in `.armisignore`
at the repo root. Suppressed CRITICAL still requires approval. See AGENTS.md for
full instructions.
